WEBVTT
TITLE Disk Scheduling — GATE Visual Explainer
NOTE Timings are estimated from the lesson timeline (speaking-rate based), not measured from recorded audio.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
A disk is a stack of concentric tracks, and one arm reads all of them.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
One access costs seek + rotational latency + transfer: 10 + 4.17 + 0.04 ms.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Only the seek is under the scheduler control, so the topic is head movement.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Eight requests arrive in this order; FCFS serves them in exactly that order.

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Total movement 640 cylinders: 45 + 85 + 146 + 85 + 108 + 110 + 59 + 2.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
FCFS never starves anyone, and pays for it with the longest travel.

7
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
SSTF always serves the nearest pending request.

8
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Same queue, 236 cylinders: 12 + 2 + 30 + 23 + 84 + 24 + 2 + 59.

9
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
The far request at 183 waits while nearer ones keep arriving.

10
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Greedy is not optimal. Head at 50, requests 11, 40, 60 and 90.

11
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:50.000
SSTF goes 40, 60, 90, 11 and travels 139 cylinders.

12
00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:00.000
The order 11, 40, 60, 90 travels 118. Nearest-first lost by 21.

13
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:10.000
SCAN keeps one direction until the end of the disk, then reverses.

14
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Upward from 53: 65, 67, 98, 122, 124, 183, 199, then back to 37 and 14: 331.

15
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.000
The trip to 199 is part of the definition: 16 cylinders of pure waste here.

16
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:40.000
C-SCAN returns to cylinder 0 without servicing anything on the way.

17
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:50.000
382 cylinders: 146 up to 199, the 199-cylinder jump, then 37 more.

18
00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:00.000
The jump costs movement, and buys equal treatment for the middle.

19
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:10.000
LOOK reverses at the last request instead of the end of the disk: 299.

20
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:20.000
C-LOOK jumps to the smallest pending request: 322.

21
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:30.000
GATE 2016: C-LOOK from 63 gives 24 + 5 + 29 + 70 + 181 + 1 + 27 + 9 = 346.

22
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:40.000
GATE 2015 Set 1: 100 tracks, head at 50, nine requests including 50 itself.

23
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:50.000
SSTF gives 130, SCAN toward 100 gives 140, and LOOK would give 120.

24
00:03:50.000 --> 00:04:00.000
The key is 10. Read additional as a magnitude, and notice 50 costs nothing.

25
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Movement is not always the whole cost: GATE 2018 charges per cylinder and per reversal.

26
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:20.000
SSTF from 80: 200 cylinders and 3 reversals, so 40 + 45 = 85 mW.

27
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Seek time is movement times a constant; a reversal can cost separately.

28
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:40.000
Fix the disk range, the head position and the direction before anything else.

29
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:50.000
Then write the service order, and sum the absolute differences.

30
00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Five traps: the end visit, the direction, the jump, the units, and ties.

